{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/451514-are-there-any-anime-that-look-a-lot-like-cwod-games","id":451514,"title":"are there any anime that look a lot like cwod games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-21T07:54:15-07:00","id":451514,"title":"are there any anime that look a lot like cwod games?","content":"for example shiki( i recommend it to vtm fans) is a fine example of what would happen if a sabbat pack were to visit a small isolated village","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:14:09-07:00","id":451964,"title":"","content":"Darker Than Black is what a lot of H:tR Edges probably look like. Do something weird as the trigger, and it activates a power that can save your ass (or kill you, if you lean on it inappropriately like the guy with the burgers who could move at superspeed). <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J2qVxDsbCLI\" target=\"_blank\">Hazuki Mina's laser blade ability</a> is often how I picture the use of Cleave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T16:53:20-07:00","id":452143,"title":"","content":"Requiem from the Darkness<br /> <br /> Paranoia Agent<br /> <br /> Boggipop Phantom <br /> <br /> A certain magical index: for mage players<br /> <br /> Black Lagoon: VTM without the vampires<br /> <br /> Demon Lord Dante<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T17:17:48-07:00","id":452157,"title":"","content":"Tokyo Ghoul for Vampire: the Masquerade and Kindred of the East. Only just begun watching the series but I've seen some definite inspiration for games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T17:26:45-07:00","id":452162,"title":"","content":"The Gehenna sourcebook for VtM recommends Neon Genesis Evangelion as inspirational viewing material. It's pretty spot-on for capturing the feel of ultrapowerful Biblical beings duking it out in an apocalyptic setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T19:41:36-07:00","id":452221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/451514-are-there-any-anime-that-look-a-lot-like-cwod-games?p=452162#post452162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gehenna sourcebook for VtM recommends Neon Genesis Evangelion as inspirational viewing material. It's pretty spot-on for capturing the feel of ultrapowerful Biblical beings duking it out in an apocalyptic setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you sit around and just watch the spectacle unfold - and so do your characters! (^VVVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T10:00:08-07:00","id":452787,"title":"","content":"perhaps another anime trinity blood. granted the similarities are not so big but byzantium does remind me of the dream of michael in vampire the dark ages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T21:38:33-07:00","id":453793,"title":"","content":"It has always been my theory that Alucard of Hellsing Ultimate is a 4th generation Tzimisce. There's a gambling/illusionist character that has noticeable Ravnos feel to him and there is also a concept of vampiric frenzy and a younger vampire with unexplained animal features. I also based one character on Zorin Blitz, who is... frightening and demonstrates what a really powerful Malkavian might be able to do.<br /> <br /> Still, be warned, it's an extremely graphic series. (Also, Hellsing Ultimate Abridged by the Team Four Star guys is a really good laugh.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:26:57-07:00","id":454718,"title":"","content":"There are a number of older Anime and movies that fit the bill quite nicely. I recall wanting to play Ascension pretty badly after watching Demon City Shinjuku. Actually, most movies from that era are pretty perfect if not for material then for tone: Ghost in the Shell &amp; Akira are common standbys. Going lesser know there are shows like Shamanic Princess, Cyber City Oedo 808, or Wolf's Rain. The list goes on, but that's all the comes off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T19:11:19-07:00","id":455228,"title":"","content":"I'd say the Eccentric Family is very changeling even if Tanuki and Tengu don't match up to Cwod canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T20:13:06-07:00","id":455298,"title":"","content":"Mentioned above, but I really like Wolf's Rain for its Werewolf feel. Setting-wise, it makes me think more of a post apocalyptic setting where the Garou already lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T04:27:03-07:00","id":455658,"title":"","content":"I've been gearing up for a Changeling game, so I was thinking about stuff for inspiration for that series at least.<br /> <br /> Amagai Brilliant Park and Chuunibyou are both pretty good inspirational sources for Changeling the Dreaming. Amagai Brilliant Park involves faeries from another world who have to subsist on joyful human emotions, so they run a giant amusement park to attract people, which wouldn't be impossible for a group of Changelings to do - some place like that might be a cool location for your freehold.<br /> <br /> In Chuunibyou several of the characters think that they're powerful witches, demons or angels (they're just normal people) but sometimes when they fight or do action scenes, they have cool magical battles and such (in reality they're swinging around umbrellas and soup ladles, but in their minds they're throwing out all sorts of cool attacks) and it's very easy to imagine the characters as Changelings and viewing their cool supernatural stuff as actually happening.<br /> <br /> The visual novel Umineko: When They Cry (the anime series was pretty terrible and just ends halfway through the storyline) is a fantastic example of Changeling the Dreaming. The primary themes are things like reality, banality, imagination and hope. It's also very meta-textual, in that while one story is happening, much of that is part of another story (similar to how you have two worlds in Changeling), plus it's magic system matches up rather nicely with Changeling. Indeed, it's probably the closest thing I've read to a Changeling the Dreaming story.<br /> <br /> <br /> More generically the Fate franchise (Fate/Zero, Fate/Stay Night, and other stories in the same universe like Tsukihime or Kara no Kyoukai) involve a world with mages, who hide their powers from normal humans, vampires who secretly feed on people, church inquisitions to hunt down those who reveal the secrets of the supernatural to normal people, etc. The setting has a lot in common with the World of Darkness and it's not hard to grab something from there to use as inspiration.<br /> <br /> Finally there's Dance in the Vampire Bund (the anime was it's own original adaptation and rather different from the manga). In this series an ancient, powerful and ludicrously wealthy vampire purchases all of Japan's national debt. In exchange, Japan allows her to purchase an island where she can set up her own, largely separate nation with its own laws, where vampires will be allowed to openly live (the Vampire Bund). She has a werewolf for a bodyguard, and the series has a good mix of action and political maneuvering. It's not a great fit for Vampire, but you can probably find something in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-25-2015, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T07:15:04-07:00","id":458978,"title":"","content":"mirai nikki.<br /> <br /> it's a perfect representation of the yama kings or antedilluvians fighting each other for the throne of god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T01:51:37-07:00","id":462028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/451514-are-there-any-anime-that-look-a-lot-like-cwod-games?p=455298#post455298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mentioned above, but I really like Wolf's Rain for its Werewolf feel. Setting-wise, it makes me think more of a post apocalyptic setting where the Garou already lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got that impression, too. A group of (were)wolves, running through a post-apocalyptic world, seeking a fabled paradise. And all the while, hunters and vampiric technomages pursue them. . .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:51:34-07:00","id":462694,"title":"","content":"Supernatural: The Anime - Hunters Hunted<br /> Tokyo Ghoul - Freak Legions/Book of the Wyrm (seriously people, he has Formori abilities)<br /> Wolf's Rain - Werewolf<br /> Trinity Blood - Vampire/Inquisition<br /> Dance at the Vampire Bund - Vampire for Herbert the Pervert","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}